### Errors

- Check every changed declaration with the project's linter or in the rendered page: the browser silently drops an invalid declaration, and nothing reports it.
- Give a `var()` a fallback wherever its custom property may be undefined (`color: var(--surface, #fff)`); without one, the property is treated as `unset`, discarding any earlier declaration.
- Guard a feature some of the project's browser targets lack with `@supports`, and keep a working declaration outside the guard so every target renders.
<!-- Project-specific / CSS-Errors -->

